That's one heck of a tirade based on completely false information.

Locked shop doors are not treated any differently from any other locked
doors; they can remain locked forever and they don't automatically
unlock at any point.

If they are unlocked somehow, it has no relation to the engraving in
front of them.  Erasing the engraving does not cause the door to
unlock, nor does any method of unlocking cause the engraving to be
erased (other than the normal effects of taking actions while standing
on a dust engraving).

You can check this in wizard mode, or you can look at the source and
see that the shop code only references locked doors twice: once to make
sure that if _any_ trap is generated on a door, it's merely a locked
door, and the second to make sure that if the door is locked then it
has the "Closed for inventory" engraving in front of it.  There's
nothing to unlock them after any period of time.

You could also search this newsgroup's archives to get this information.



